  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607196900: PostgreSQL pool-return session reset

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

Every reusable PostgreSQL channel must pass `pg_session_reset` before it may be
returned to an idle pool. The `.kotoba` provider first issues ROLLBACK and
drains ReadyForQuery, then issues DISCARD ALL and again drains ReadyForQuery.
Either protocol, SQLSTATE or framing failure makes the channel ineligible for
reuse and the pool must close it.

The query response parser admits bounded NoticeResponse and ParameterStatus
messages because ROLLBACK outside a transaction and DISCARD-induced setting
changes may emit them. Both reuse the existing exact field/status validators;
they do not broaden accepted arbitrary server messages.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification dirties application_name, creates a
temporary table and named prepared statement, opens a transaction and writes a
row. Reset rolls back and discards the session. The proof requires the setting
to return to default, the temp relation to disappear, the prepared statement
to fail with `26000`, a fresh query to succeed and all handles to close.

This establishes the pool-return invariant. The opaque pool lease table,
credential/certificate rotation, compatibility matrices and soak remain
open.")))
